<title>USA: BPA offers only off peak, non-firm power for Wed.</title>
<headline>BPA offers only off peak, non-firm power for Wed.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offered only non-firm power during off-peak hours for Wednesday pre-schedulings, the agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>For the previous day, BPA had offered 200 MW of peak firm power at $16.00-18.00 per megawatt hour (MWh).</p>
<p>BPA's prices for non-firm Wednesday sales were unchanged at $8.00 for all deliveries during hours ending ending 0100-0500 and 2400 PDT.</p>
<p>Non-firm power at hours ending 0600 and 2300 on Wednesday was unchanged at $10.00, while prices for hours ending 0700-0800 were steady $13.00 per MWh for Northwest sales and $14.00 for COB.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau, +1 213 955 6761))</p>
